msgid ""
"title: Quickstart\n"
"description: A quickstart guide for the Shaded lightcones Qiskit addon (qiskit-addon-slc)\n"
msgstr ""
"title: Quickstart\n"
"description: Isang quickstart guide para sa Shaded lightcones Qiskit addon (qiskit-addon-slc)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide demonstrates a minimal working example of the `qiskit-addon-slc` package. It calculates a shaded lightcone to reduce the sampling cost of probabilistic error cancellation (PEC).\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng gabay na ito ang isang minimal na gumaganang halimbawa ng package na `qiskit-addon-slc`. Kinakalkula nito ang isang shaded lightcone para bawasan ang sampling cost ng probabilistic error cancellation (PEC).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC mitigates gate noise by sampling from a quasiprobability decomposition of the inverse noise channel. Its sampling cost grows with every error term it must mitigate; however, not every error affects the observable equally. An error outside the observable's causal lightcone cannot influence the measured expectation value, and even within the lightcone, some errors are more detrimental than others. A shaded lightcone quantifies this by bounding the effect each Pauli error term has on the observable. Truncating the error terms with the smallest effect shrinks the noise model that PEC has to mitigate, reducing sampling cost in exchange for a small, bounded bias.\n"
msgstr "Minimitigate ng PEC ang gate noise sa pamamagitan ng pag-sample mula sa isang quasiprobability decomposition ng inverse noise channel. Lumalaki ang sampling cost nito sa bawat error term na kailangan nitong i-mitigate; gayunpaman, hindi pantay ang epekto ng bawat error sa observable. Ang error na nasa labas ng causal lightcone ng observable ay hindi makakaimpluwensya sa sinukat na expectation value, at kahit sa loob ng lightcone, may mga error na mas nakakasama kaysa sa iba. Kinukwantipika ito ng isang shaded lightcone sa pamamagitan ng pag-bound sa epekto ng bawat Pauli error term sa observable. Ang pag-truncate sa mga error term na may pinakamaliit na epekto ay nagpapaliit sa noise model na kailangang i-mitigate ng PEC, na binabawasan ang sampling cost kapalit ng maliit at may hangganang bias.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see how to build a realistic workflow and run on quantum hardware, check out the [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones) tutorial on IBM Quantum Platform.\n"
msgstr "Para makita kung paano bumuo ng makatotohanang workflow at tumakbo sa quantum hardware, tingnan ang tutorial na [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones) sa IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Prepare the inputs for SLC {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-slc}"
msgstr "1. Ihanda ang mga input para sa SLC {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-slc}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, build a 10-qubit Trotterized transverse-field Ising circuit and choose a single-qubit $Z$ observable on the middle qubit.\n"
msgstr "Una, bumuo ng 10-qubit na Trotterized transverse-field Ising circuit at pumili ng single-qubit na $Z$ observable sa gitnang qubit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart/extracted-outputs/0fff4e37-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart/extracted-outputs/0fff4e37-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SLC operates on the noisy two-qubit-gate layers of the circuit. Here we use ``samplomatic`` to group the gates into annotated boxes and attach a noise-injection annotation to each two-qubit layer. SLC requires every noisy box to have a unique `modifier_ref`, which `inject_noise_strategy=\"individual_modification\"` provides; with samplomatic's default strategy, the bounds come out wrong or their computation never finishes. `generate_noise_model_paulis` then enumerates the Pauli error terms of every unique noisy layer.\n"
msgstr "Gumagana ang SLC sa mga noisy na layer ng two-qubit-gate ng circuit. Dito, ginagamit natin ang ``samplomatic`` para i-grupo ang mga gate sa mga annotated na box at maglagay ng noise-injection annotation sa bawat two-qubit layer. Kailangan ng SLC na may natatanging `modifier_ref` ang bawat noisy box, na ibinibigay ng `inject_noise_strategy=\"individual_modification\"`; sa default na strategy ng samplomatic, mali ang lalabas na mga bound o hindi natatapos ang pagkalkula nito. Pagkatapos, binibilang ng `generate_noise_model_paulis` ang mga Pauli error term ng bawat natatanging noisy layer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Compute the shaded lightcone {#2-compute-the-shaded-lightcone}"
msgstr "2. Kalkulahin ang shaded lightcone {#2-compute-the-shaded-lightcone}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The shaded lightcone is assembled by assigning a scale to each Pauli error term in the noise model based on how much effect it has on the observable expectation value. These scales are derived from each error term's forward and backward error bounds (described below), as well as its error rate:\n"
msgstr "Binubuo ang shaded lightcone sa pamamagitan ng pagtatalaga ng scale sa bawat Pauli error term sa noise model batay sa kung gaano kalaki ang epekto nito sa expectation value ng observable. Nakukuha ang mga scale na ito mula sa forward at backward na error bound ng bawat error term (inilalarawan sa ibaba), pati na rin sa error rate nito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_forward_bounds` evolves each error term *forward* to the end of the circuit to bound its effect on the observable measured there.\n"
msgstr "Ineebolb ng `compute_forward_bounds` ang bawat error term *pasulong* hanggang sa dulo ng circuit para i-bound ang epekto nito sa observable na sinusukat doon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_backward_bounds` evolves each error term *backward* to the start of the circuit to bound its effect on the initial state.\n"
msgstr "Ineebolb ng `compute_backward_bounds` ang bawat error term *paatras* hanggang sa simula ng circuit para i-bound ang epekto nito sa initial state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge_bounds` combines the two into a single bound per error term. Each bound is scaled by the term's error rate. These rates typically come from a noise learning experiment (such as `NoiseLearnerV3`); this guide uses random rates for simplicity.\n"
msgstr "Pinagsasama ng `merge_bounds` ang dalawa sa isang bound kada error term. Ang bawat bound ay sinusukat ayon sa error rate ng term. Karaniwang galing ang mga rate na ito sa isang noise learning experiment (gaya ng `NoiseLearnerV3`); gumagamit ang gabay na ito ng mga random na rate para sa pagiging simple.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the shaded lightcone visualization below, each box is shaded by how strongly the errors at that site can affect the observable.  Bright boxes carry the largest bounds, while boxes that fade to the background contain error terms that have little effect on the calculation -- these errors are natural candidates to drop from the noise model. The values in the visualization below represent sums of the error bounds of all Pauli errors at that site, which is why some of the values grow larger than ``2.0``, the bound for any single Pauli error.\n"
msgstr "Sa visualization ng shaded lightcone sa ibaba, ang bawat box ay may shade ayon sa kung gaano kalakas makaaapekto ang mga error sa site na iyon sa observable.  Ang mga maliwanag na box ang may pinakamalalaking bound, habang ang mga box na lumalabo papunta sa background ay may mga error term na kaunti lang ang epekto sa kalkulasyon -- natural na kandidato ang mga error na ito para tanggalin sa noise model. Ang mga halaga sa visualization sa ibaba ay kumakatawan sa mga kabuuan ng error bound ng lahat ng Pauli error sa site na iyon, kaya may ilang halaga na lumalaki nang higit sa ``2.0``, ang bound para sa anumang iisang Pauli error.\n"

