# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Reduce the sampling cost {#3-reduce-the-sampling-cost}"
msgstr "3. Bawasan ang sampling cost {#3-reduce-the-sampling-cost}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_local_scales` turns the shaded lightcone into a concrete PEC configuration. It prioritizes error terms by their bounded effect on the observable and truncates the least impactful ones until the requested `bias_tolerance` is reached. It returns scales for each error term: `0.0` for terms to ignore during mitigation and `-1.0` for terms that should be mitigated. The function also returns the resulting **sampling cost** overhead ($\\gamma^2$) and a bound on the **residual bias** incurred by the truncation.\n"
msgstr "Ginagawa ng `compute_local_scales` na konkretong PEC configuration ang shaded lightcone. Inuuna nito ang mga error term ayon sa naka-bound nilang epekto sa observable at tina-truncate ang mga pinakakaunti ang epekto hanggang maabot ang hiniling na `bias_tolerance`. Nagbabalik ito ng mga scale para sa bawat error term: `0.0` para sa mga term na babalewalain sa mitigation at `-1.0` para sa mga term na dapat i-mitigate. Ibinabalik din ng function ang nagresultang overhead ng **sampling cost** ($\\gamma^2$) at isang bound sa **residual bias** na dulot ng pag-truncate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `bias_tolerance=0.0` mitigates every error term within the causal lightcone of the observable and gives a baseline sampling cost. Allowing a small bias lets SLC drop the low-impact terms and reduce that cost further.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagtatakda ng `bias_tolerance=0.0` ay nagmi-mitigate sa bawat error term sa loob ng causal lightcone ng observable at nagbibigay ng baseline na sampling cost. Kapag pinayagan ang maliit na bias, maaaring tanggalin ng SLC ang mga term na mababa ang epekto at higit pang bawasan ang cost na iyon.\n"
